{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>For he told them that he is a Jew.</b> For it is forbidden to him. Now one may ask: why did Mordecai put himself in danger, and put all Israel in danger too? It would have been fitting that he speak to Esther, and she would remove him from the king's gate, and not anger Haman, since he saw that the hour was playing into his hand. The answer: he could not withdraw from the king's gate, for if he withdraws without the king's command, his blood is on his head."], :book :esther, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Kol Sason, Krotoschin, 1840" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001728315"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:29:53.317571006Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}